course: dictionary
lesson: 6487
title: A word with a painful history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words carry a heavy history inside them, and «nazi» is one of them. It names a member of the political party led by Adolf Hitler, which ruled Germany before and during World War Two. The context tells you what it means: «Adolf Hitler and the Nazi Party took power in Germany in 1933, ended free elections and free speech, and persecuted Jews and others.»
explain: Look at the clues: took power, ended free elections, persecuted others. These words show that the Nazis were cruel and dangerous, not harmless. When you meet «Nazi», ask what the sentence is about. In history lessons, it is usually about war, cruelty and the Holocaust.
explain: «The Nazis murdered about six million Jews, as well as many Roma, disabled people and others, only because of who they were; this is called the Holocaust.» The context shows this is a serious word about real people who suffered. It is never a word to use for fun.
fact: «Nazi» is a noun for a member of the Nazi Party, and an adjective, as in «Nazi Germany».
fact: The Nazis ruled Germany from 1933 to 1945.
fact: «Holocaust» is the name for the Nazi murder of Europe's Jews.
fact: The Nazis murdered about six million Jews, as well as many Roma, disabled people and others.
fact: Some people use «nazi» as an insult for a very strict person. This is careless, and it can upset people, especially those whose families lived through the Holocaust.
exercise: «The Nazis ruled Germany from 1933 to 1945.» Who were the Nazis? | A friendly club of football fans | *A political party led by Adolf Hitler | A country in Africa | A kind of old car
exercise: «At Babyn Yar, Nazi forces murdered about 33,771 Jews in two days in September 1941.» What does murdered show? | *A cruel killing of people | A lost ball | A kind act | A party game
exercise: Ben calls his teacher a «grammar nazi». Why is this careless? | It is a long word | It means a grammar expert, so it is always polite | It is only used in Germany | *It makes light of the murder of millions of people
test: «The Holocaust was the Nazi murder of Europe's Jews.» What is the Holocaust? | A famous football club | A kind of holiday | *The Nazi murder of Europe's Jews | A German city
test: In the phrase «Nazi Germany», what does Nazi tell you? | It tells you the country is very small | *It tells you the country was ruled by the Nazi Party | It tells you the country is a football team | It tells you the country has no roads
exam: Why do we remember the Holocaust? | To make jokes about strict teachers | *So we remember the millions murdered and work to make sure such cruelty never happens again | To learn how to play board games | To choose a name for a new park
